source: apps/cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "run(&[\"--help\"]).transcript()"
---
exit code: 0
--- stdout
Turn data into structured, navigable sound.

Exit codes: 0 success, 1 errors, 2 usage, 3 warnings denied. Every command accepts --json for machine-readable output and --plain for linear text without colour or box drawing (screen readers).

Usage: sonarithm [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  validate  Check a spec: syntax, shape, meaning, and the defaults it will get
  inspect   Compile a spec; print the Score summary, a description and the diagnostics
  lint      Compile a spec and report its warnings with rule IDs (a stub until the perceptual lint arrives in C05)
  quick     Sonify one data file with the default design: x along time, y as pitch
  schema    Print a JSON Schema
  spec      Work on spec files
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON on standard output, with stable field names

      --plain
          Print linear text: no colour, no box drawing, progress as text lines

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
--- stderr
